      "bottomRightX": 587,
      "bottomRightY": 824,
      "content": "and quantum multiplication is not commutative, although, as is easily verified, it is associative and distributive. The quantity with components $xy (nm)$ defined by (2) we shall call the Heisenberg product of $x$ and $y$, and shall write simply as $xy$. Whenever two quantum quantities occur multiplied together, the Heisenberg product will be understood. Ordinary multiplication is, of course, implied in the products of amplitudes and frequencies and other quantities that are related to sets of $n$'s which are explicitly stated.",
